graphify-out/
# The dev split dumped to disk by `bench/fixture.py`, so the extractor can be
# written without the corpus generator. Regenerated from the committed seed,
# and the committed checksum is what says it has not moved — committing the
# dump as well would be a second copy of the corpus that could disagree.
bench/fixture-dev/
# claude-code-log's MIT fixtures, cloned by whoever wants to run the 322
# conformance cases. The default used to be a directory in `/tmp`, which is a
# scratch path this project bans in its documentation for the reason it then
# proved: the clone outlived the sentence quoting it and not much longer, and
# the README's test count silently depended on it. Repo-local and ignored, so
# it survives a reboot and ships nowhere. [E7 pair review]
.conformance/
# Review agents are given a git worktree of their own, which lands here. A
# worktree is a checkout, so git offers to commit it as a gitlink — and did,
# once. Their scratch is theirs; it is not this repository's history.
.claude/
